+/// How many RPC connections to the node to keep.
+///
+/// Each one is a socket, and each is a slot for work that would otherwise queue behind whatever
+/// else is talking to the node. Four rather than more because every slot can become peer
+/// connections opened by the proxy in front of a pruned node, and a node has only so many peers
+/// worth asking: eight outbound full-relay peers is typical, and this is bounded well under that
+/// even with the proxy's own per-block concurrency on top.
+///
+/// It is also the ceiling on concurrent RPCs reaching the node at all, which several clients being
+/// served at once (`server.rs`) would otherwise leave unbounded. Comfortable against bitcoind's
+/// own `rpcthreads`, which the packaged node defaults to 16 and will not let you set below 4.
+const RPC_POOL_SIZE: usize = 4;
+
